Fittings, bends, junctions and what a loss coefficient means (@fd-fittings: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18", #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-and-Engineering-Chakraborty.lingua#r_31BBWRVBVVYRX6MZNTND5FZYF2", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ", #fluid-dynamics "Pump-curves-operating-points-and-connected-fluid-networks.lingua#r_38PV7C2PG9F67V9SENTE32AD5Y") { r_44H4W4CTXATB85WBAMMY1BN8WK
**Read:** [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18), internal-flow losses and momentum applications; [Introduction to Fluid Mechanics and Fluid Engineering — Suman Chakraborty](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-and-Engineering-Chakraborty.lingua#r_31BBWRVBVVYRX6MZNTND5FZYF2), expansion, fittings and pipe-system lectures; [Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ), control-volume and loss problems.

A local-loss model writes h_L=K U_ref²/(2g). The reference velocity, location of pressure measurements and inclusion of downstream recovery belong to the definition of K. Calling a fitting a minor loss does not mean its contribution is small. Closely spaced disturbances can interact, so adding isolated coefficients is an assumption to examine.

Derive a sudden-expansion estimate using mass, momentum and mechanical energy under the model's assumptions; for the idealized fully mixed endpoints its loss is (U_1−U_2)²/(2g). Explain why static-pressure recovery can occur while total mechanical head decreases. For a junction, maintain each branch's mass and energy account and distinguish a loss coefficient from force on the pipe supports.

Compare two independently documented coefficients only after matching geometry, Reynolds number, opening and reference speed. An installed valve's position is not automatically a reproducible flow resistance. Design observations that separate straight-pipe resistance from a fitting's loss and identify when a three-dimensional flow calculation or direct test is justified.

**Continue:** [Pump curves, operating points and connected fluid networks](Pump-curves-operating-points-and-connected-fluid-networks.lingua#r_38PV7C2PG9F67V9SENTE32AD5Y).

